l":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1706327789","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/35692#issuecomment-1706327789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/35692","id":1706327789,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCFbutM5ltH7t","user":{"login":"msavy","id":423513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzUxMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/423513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy","html_url":"https://github.com/msavy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-05T10:08:11Z","updated_at":"2023-09-05T10:09:13Z","body":"> > > and this JUnit callback is invoked for each test method by default, i.e. with @testinstance(Lifecycle.PER_TEST)\r\n> > \r\n> > \r\n> > Ah... I guess we will have to rely on our state in that case...\r\n> \r\n> Can't we just move the invocation of `QuarkusTestBeforeClassCallback` in the `QuarkusTestExtension.beforeAll()` method?\r\n\r\nI've already tried that locally and using the `beforeAll` JUnit5 callback works fine (I can submit a PR).\r\n\r\nThe only question in my mind is whether \"before class callback\" is actually a different use case to \"before all\"? \r\n\r\nClearly, the existing documentation doesn't match today's behaviour and suggests it is meant to be `@BeforeAll` — and none of the existing Quarkus callbacks provide the necessary `@BeforeAll` functionality. But, given the way that JUnit works (i.e. it always reinstantiates the class before each method call), would there be any reason we need both? \r\n\r\nI suspect any other use cases are already covered by the existing callbacks (before each, after constructor, etc), so it should be safe to make the change — but I just wanted to put that out there as a point to consider.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1706327789/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"msavy","id":423513,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzUxMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/423513?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy","html_url":"https://github.com/msavy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msavy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":10281653016,"node_id":"MEE_lADOCFbutM5v8iWzzwAAAAJk1ZMY","url"